{
  "issue_date": "2025-10-09",
  "report_week": 41,
  "year": 2025,
  "quote_of_the_week": {
    "type": "Quote of the Week",
    "quote": "Tough times don't' last, but tough people do.",
    "author": "Margaret Devereaux - fictional character from the American crime drama tv series \"Tulsa King"
  },
  "market_commentary": {
    "overview": "",
    "bulkers": "Despite the subdued s+p activity leading up to Wednesday (end of Far Eastern holidays), \nthere were a notable number of transactions that were likely concluded prior to the break and have now \nbeen revealed to the market: 1 Newcastlemax, 4 Kamsarmaxes, 2 Panamaxes, 1 Ultramax, 4 \nSupramaxes & 6 handysize bulkers changed hands at firm levels. \n \nOverall, the dry-cargo chartering market is healthy, despite the holidays in the Far East; at a glance, the \nAtlantic market shows strength with rates ranging from $22k to $25k for Handies and Supras. The \nIndian Ocean market is experiencing a slight decline with rates in the region of $11k to $13k for \nHandies and Supras. Meanwhile, the Far East period rates are exceeding 15k for Supras and Ultras.",
    "tankers": "Two en bloc deals are attracting the attention this week; a pair of scrubber-fitted 160k built \n2012 & 2013 HHIC/Philippines Suezmaxes changed hands for $90 mill, in the meantime Abu Dhabi \nbuyers paid a substantial $122.4 mill for a pair of 109k built 2019 New Times/China Aframax Sisters.",
    "demolition": "The markets in the subcontinent are generally stable, except for Bangladesh, where a \nrebound is expected. For an overview of demolition market rates this week, please check our \ncomprehensive demometer below:"
  },
  "baltic_indices": [],
